      "message": "fix(geometry): re-triage the STEP pins that solidcore fa67b3f5 moves\n\nThe new Part 21 parser holds a text's counts to a density of its own\nlength. step_diag probes each DATA record alone in a short frame, so a\ndense legal record was refused as a syntax error. Read the density\nrefusals (TooManyParams, TooManyRecords, TooManyEntities) of the probe\nas no syntax fault; the parse of the whole file keeps the limits.\n\nMoved pins, each still a refusal or an exact measure:\n- twisted_flank_off.step: refused at the vertex check, not at read.\n- edge_gap_021_stated_5mm.step: refused at read by the gap check (cap\n  0.02 mm named), not at the mesh chord.\n- cube-chamfer-all-12-d2: 808 mm3, mitred corners (upstream #21269).\n- machining_mesh_shortfalls case 3: NotWatertight, not Lenient (#3800).\n\nRefs #3767\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
